Local review patch: preflight before accepting the complete cached T6032 inventory
Base: reviewed m1n1 2460b604c6f016956ead711823605eea840c602e, after adapted 0005
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Keep the full 32-node, two-die validation before reset-state publication or
startup. Populate upstream's CPU/node caches only after the entire inventory
passes, and do not reparse it with legacy scalar getters or arm-io fallback.
Other SoCs retain upstream parsing. No hardware access occurs in preflight.
This is all-or-nothing validation, not an atomic concurrent memcpy primitive.
RVBAR, MPIDR/entry state, reset ordering and native qualification remain open.
This comparison series retains upstream dispatch and is not boot-approved.

